The purpose of this study is to identify the causes of accidents and obstacles based on the current state of urban railway accidents caused by human errors that occur continuously, to identify the causes of human errors in urban railway crews, The purpose of this paper is to propose a practical human error mitigation plan and to improve the desirable railway safety culture through the empirical analysis. Also, it will improve the satisfaction of citizen users through efficient management of urban railway accidents and enhance the efficiency of human resources management in the organization. It has its purpose.&#xD;
  In order to carry out this study, we suggest the subculture factors and human error induction factors of the crew through the theoretical examination of the job stress and the railway safety culture which are identified as the main causes of human error. The results of this study were obtained through statistical analysis to clarify the effect of job stress on the safety culture of railway.&#xD;
  The data survey and analysis methodology was constructed by using the survey tool based on the research of the previous research and the questionnaire survey was conducted among the crew members who are currently working at Seoul Transportation Corporation (lines 1 to 4) The results of this study are summarized as follows. First, the results of this study are as follows. The questionnaire consisted of 155 people with accidents and disabilities who were working at Seoul Transportation Corporation (lines1~4). The analysis was conducted using SPSS18.0 statistical program.&#xD;
